                <head>No. 459.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pendleton.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, Berlin:</hi></p>
                <p>The President desires you to make expression through the foreign office of the
                    respectful sympathy felt throughout the United States for the German nation in
                    the loss of their Emperor, who has at last yielded to death with such lofty
                    courage and calm resignation to the divine decree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
